data: {"type":"block","block":{"type":"WritingDraft","id":"turn-086d335aaf67-writing-draft","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"data":{"kind":"literature_review","title":"Retrieval in retrieval-augmented generation: sources, processes and evaluation","sections":[{"heading":"What is retrieved and how","segments":[{"text":"The survey describes retrieval sources as widening from plain text to semi-structured and structured data. It also notes a growing use of content generated by LLMs themselves.","citationIds":["c1"],"speaker":null},{"text":"Several sources describe combining retrieval approaches. A survey lists hybrid strategies that mix keyword, semantic and vector search. The graph-based work pairs rule-following symbolic retrievers with embedding-based neural ones.","citationIds":["c2","c3"],"speaker":null}]},{"heading":"Single-pass versus multi-step retrieval","segments":[{"text":"The survey contrasts the common single retrieval pass with iterative retrieval. Iterative retrieval repeatedly searches the knowledge base using the query and the text generated so far, and is said to make later answers more robust.","citationIds":["c4"],"speaker":null},{"text":"Adaptive retrieval goes further by letting the system decide whether retrieval is needed and when to stop. Methods such as FLARE and Self-RAG are presented as moving beyond a fixed retrieval process.","citationIds":["c4","c2"],"speaker":null}]},{"heading":"Evaluation and open questions","segments":[{"text":"Evaluation practice varies between studies. One chunking study says recall is usually the main retrieval metric but argues that its setup also needs precision and F1. A graph-memory study instead reports recall@2 and recall@5 against baselines such as BM25, Contriever, GTR and ColBERTv2.","citationIds":["c5","c6"],"speaker":null}]}],"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f22af6d01a52a8fb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"there is also a growing trend in recent researches towards utilizing content generated by LLMs themselves for retrieval and enhancement purposes."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_445a807c7c2b8b50","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"Hybrid retrieval strategies integrate keyword, semantic, and vector searches to cater to diverse queries."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_9d1c3f70428d0475","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":35,"quote":"Meanwhile, the neural retriever complements this by using embedding-based similarity, capturing nuanced patterns and contextual relationships that may not be directly encoded in rules."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_18d9f568d1c19f4e","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":10,"quote":"Iterative retrieval is a process where the knowledge base is repeatedly searched based on the initial query and the text generated so far"},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_26249f4bdc41b629","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":9,"quote":"In typical retrieval experiments, recall is often the primary metric."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_1561f63effe8dae8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":5,"quote":"We compare against several strong and widely used retrieval methods: BM25 [69], Contriever [35], GTR [53] and ColBERTv2 [70]."}],"bibliography":[{"docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","apa":"Retrieval Augmented Generation for Large Language Models A Survey. arXiv:2312.10997.","ieee":""Retrieval Augmented Generation for Large Language Models A Survey," arXiv:2312.10997.","bib